  "body": "Wake each morning to uninterrupted views, step aboard your boat from your own 16 metre berth, enjoy coffee at the local café, and spend your weekends boating, golfing or exploring Shakespear Regional Park—all without worrying about mowing lawns, exterior maintenance or organising trades.\r\n\r\nPositioned on the top floor, this expansive 230sqm penthouse enjoys complete privacy, all-day sunshine and expansive views. Three generous bedrooms each feature their own ensuite, while the spacious open-plan living area, dedicated office, sauna and unique belvedere create a home that is as functional as it is impressive.\r\n\r\nA secure double garage, attic storage and one of the marina’s most desirable 16 metre berths complete this exceptional offering.\r\nImportantly, this is a lifestyle where the building and grounds are professionally maintained, allowing owners to simply lock up and travel whenever they choose. For many purchasers, the annual body corporate levy replaces much of the ongoing maintenance, insurance and exterior upkeep that comes with owning a large standalone home—making life simpler, more predictable and considerably more enjoyable.\r\n\r\nThe value of your own marina berth should not be understated. 16 metre berths are a valuable commodity and highly sought after. If not intended for your own use, the yearly rental income is the perfect way to offset your outgoings. The berth (M66) owned by 35 Waterside Crescent is in a canal largely protected from excessive winds, allowing for easier berthing, and the distance from the end of the wall allows reversing in without restriction. Restricted access to marina users as well as security cameras only add to your peace of mind.\r\n\r\nThis is far more than an apartment. It’s a premium waterfront lifestyle with space, privacy and convenience that is increasingly difficult to find.",
